+# Park ordinary influence delta after experiment29
+
+Retain candidate25. Experiment29 derives a current influence map from an exact
+parent map for actual ordinary main children. A private position-bound scratch
+and predecessor factory establish both map and child provenance. Raw supplied
+maps, root/null/IIO entries and special moves retain fresh fallback; Q is unchanged.
+No persistent Node, Position or Search fields are added.
+
+The focused kernel passes179 native tests, including94 adversarial transitions
+and122 legal pairs. Integrated provenance source passes182 tests. Those finite
+pairs reduce counted profile writes9548→2327 and ray calls3012→768; these are
+conditional kernel operations, not production eligibility, traffic or CPU gain.
+Actual generic lowering retains the incremental mechanism but also materializes
+128-byte temporary/output maps and an outlined fill. Its stack/copy costs remain
+relevant despite unchanged ordinary entry allocation.
+
+The fixed70-lifetime pilot gives14.086995→14.0424665 seconds in summed native CPU
+medians (0.316097% lower), with only3/7 lower medians and worst ratio1.017434.
+It fails the frozen rule: aggregate ratio≤0.995, at least5 lower cases and worst
+ratio≤1.02. All70 original strict replay checks pass live and independently.
+No own-PGO, separate54/wire regression, full117 or12-game gate follows, and no
+source is promoted. This reported-only pilot does not establish final performance
+qualification or prescribe the cause of the small net difference.
+
+See [decision evidence](../../evidence/influence-delta-decision-20261019-01/README.md)
+and [compact checkpoint](../../evidence/influence-delta-checkpoint-20261019-01/README.md).
